\section{RT-CSI Dataset Configuration}\label{app:rt_scenarios}
  The RT-CSI benchmark is generated with NVIDIA Sionna RT~2.0.1. To construct a mixed-scene dataset for training and evaluation, we use five non-Shenzhen scenes, including Munich, Paris \'Etoile, Florence, ZJU, and SUTD. The Munich, Paris \'Etoile, and Florence layouts are the OpenStreetMap (OSM)-derived scenes released with Sionna RT, whereas the ZJU, SUTD, and Shenzhen Futian CBD layouts are constructed from OSM exports using the Blosm Blender add-on. The Shenzhen Futian CBD scene is kept as a held-out test scenario to evaluate the generalization capability of CSI feedback models under dense high-rise deployment, where strong blockage and diffuse multipath are expected. Unless otherwise specified, all scenes follow the common carrier, antenna, propagation, and normalization settings summarized in Table~\ref{tab:rt_csi_params}.

  For BS deployment, we place $N_{\text{BS}}=5$ BSs in each non-Shenzhen scene by selecting rooftop candidates ranked by height, while enforcing a minimum lateral separation between any two BSs to avoid clustering co-located transmitters. For the ZJU and SUTD campus scenes, the rooftop candidate set is further restricted to the campus bounding box. This restriction excludes nearby residential blocks in ZJU and the Singapore Expo exhibition halls adjacent to SUTD, and selects the central campus library as one of the five BSs in both campus scenes. In contrast, Shenzhen Futian CBD uses a separate held-out configuration with $N_{\text{BS}}=10$ BSs. The BS heights are constrained to $25$--$50~\mathrm{m}$ so that supertall landmarks, including the Ping An Finance Center and KK100, act as dominant blockers and scatterers rather than transmitter sites.
