\section{Conclusion}
In this letter, we have investigated the beamforming design to enhance the performance of multi-IRS-assisted wireless beam routing systems, taking into account practical near-field channel modeling. Under a beam-training-based communication protocol, the problem was formulated to maximize the received power by jointly optimizing the beamforming of the BS and intermediate IRSs. To address the formulated problem, a reformulation and an efficient AO-based algorithm were proposed. Numerical results have demonstrated that the power scaling derived under the far-field assumption no longer holds under near-field conditions. Furthermore, compared to the benchmark schemes, the proposed AO-based scheme obtains superior system performance by achieving higher received signal power at the UE.
