\subsection{Effect of the Backscatter Reflection Coefficient}
\label{subsec:eta}
The reflection coefficient $\eta_k$ controls the fraction of incident power
re-radiated by \gls{bd}$_k$ and therefore affects both the desired
backscatter signal and the interference observed by the \gls{noma} users.
To characterise this interaction, $\eta_k$ is swept over
$[0.3,0.999]$ at three intra-cluster power allocations:
$\alpha_{k,m}=0.014$, $0.05$, and $0.20$, with $M=10$ and $N=12$.
The first allocation is close to the equal-rate operating point identified
in Section~\ref{subsec:pac_fairness}, whereas $\alpha_{k,m}=0.20$
represents a more sum-rate-oriented allocation.
